1
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,040
[rain pattering] [jukebox playing]

2
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:07,400
JUNE: Kitchen closes at midnight,
mister. You want pie or not?

3
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:14,660
HALE: Cherry. And whatever you
know about the man in booth four last Tuesday.

4
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:19,160
JUNE: You a cop?

5
00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:26,200
HALE: Detective Sam Hale. A painting
worth two million walked out of the Whitmore Gallery.

6
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:31,780
JUNE: And you think it walked in
here for coffee?

7
00:01:33,780 --> 00:01:35,880
HALE: I think the man who carried it did.

8
00:01:38,880 --> 00:01:42,720
JUNE: Booth four. Gray coat. Paid
with a fifty and didn't want change.

9
00:01:45,720 --> 00:01:48,480
JUNE: He left a matchbook from
the Blue Heron Hotel.

10
00:01:57,480 --> 00:01:58,980
[door chimes]

11
00:02:00,980 --> 00:02:05,300
HALE: June, the hotel room was
empty. But there was a receipt from this diner.

12
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:10,400
JUNE: Lots of people eat here, detective.

13
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:15,700
HALE: Not lots of people sign the
receipt with your initials.

14
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:23,540
JUNE: Okay. He's my brother, Tommy.
He owed money to the wrong people.

15
00:02:26,540 --> 00:02:30,320
JUNE: They made him steal it. The
painting is in the diner's freezer.

16
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:34,820
HALE: Why tell me now?

17
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:41,980
JUNE: Because you ordered cherry
pie. Tommy's favorite. Figured you might understand family.

18
00:02:44,980 --> 00:02:47,680
HALE: I'll do what I can for him.
That's a promise.

19
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:52,680
